  {
    "title": "Unit 1: Complete Key Vocabulary & Terminology (25 Words) 📚",
    "content": "📌\n<b><font color='#007BFF'>Welcome Freshmen Students to Communicative English Skills II (EnLa102)! 👋✨</font></b>\n\nHere is the complete vocabulary list for Unit 1: Life Skills, formatted in passage-based for your study and exam preparation.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>1. Well-being (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> The state of being comfortable, healthy, or happy.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ጤንነትና ደህንነት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Welfare, Health, Happiness\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Misery, Suffering, Ill-being\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Personal responsibility involves making choices that enhance your personal well-being.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>2. Self-awareness (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Conscious knowledge of one's own character, feelings, motives, and desires.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ራስን ማወቅ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Self-knowledge, Consciousness, Mindfulness\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Ignorance, Unawareness\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Generic life skills include decision-making, problem-solving, and self-awareness.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>3. Peer pressure (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Direct influence on people by peers to change their attitudes or behaviors.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የእኩዮች ተፅዕኖ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Peer influence, Social pressure\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Individual independence\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Personal skills help young people fully understand and resist the influence of peer pressure.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>4. Self-efficacy (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> An individual's belief in their capacity to execute behaviors necessary to produce specific performance attainments.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> በራስ የመተማመን አቅም/ችሎታ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Self-confidence, Capability, Competence\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Incompetence, Self-doubt\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Life skills contribute directly to people's perceptions of self-efficacy.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>5. Self-esteem (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Confidence in one's own worth or abilities; self-respect.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> በራስ የመተማመን ስሜት/ክብር\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Self-respect, Pride, Confidence\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Self-hatred, Low self-worth\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Belonging plays a key role in the growth and development of self-esteem.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>6. Framed (Verb / Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Formulated, expressed, or defined in a particular concept or system.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የተቀረጸ፣ የተገለጸ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Formulated, Expressed, Defined\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Disorganized, Unstructured\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Life skills are framed as abilities for adaptive and positive behavior.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>7. Innumerable (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Too many to be counted.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ቁጥር የሌለው፣ እጅግ ብዙ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Countless, Infinite, Endless\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Countable, Limited, Few\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Skills that can be classified as life skills are innumerable and vary across cultures.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>8. Core (Noun / Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> The central, innermost, or most essential part of something.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ዋና፣ መሠረታዊ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Central, Essential, Fundamental\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Peripheral, Minor, Secondary\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Analysis shows there is a core set of skills at the heart of health promotion initiatives.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>9. Kinship (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> A sharing of characteristics or origins; a feeling of close connection or relationship.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የሥጋ ዝምድና፣ የቅርበት ስሜት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Connection, Affinity, Bond\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Estrangement, Alienation\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Human nature includes a strong innate potential for kinship and belonging.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>10. Pursue (Verb)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Seek to attain or accomplish a goal over a period of time.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> መከተል፣ ማሳደድ፣ መፈለግ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Seek, Follow, Strive for\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Abandon, Give up, Shun\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Belonging gives individuals the ability to pursue meaningful relationships in society.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>11. Livelihood (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> A means of securing the necessities of life.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የዕለት ተዕለት ኑሮ/መተዳደሪያ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Living, Income, Maintenance\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Entertainment, Hobby\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> The term life skills is sometimes used to refer to livelihood skills like setting up a business.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>12. Interpersonal (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Relating to relationships or communication between people.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የሰዎች እርስ በእርስ ግንኙነት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Social, Relational, Interactive\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Intrapersonal, Individual\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Life skills help students build effective interpersonal relationships and resolve conflicts.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>13. Competently (Adverb)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> In an efficient, capable, and suitable manner.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> በብቃት፣ በተስማሚ ሁኔታ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Capably, Efficiently, Skillfully\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Incompetently, Poorly\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Young people need social skills to function confidently and competently in their community.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>14. Adaptive (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Able to adjust or change to suit different conditions or environments.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ሁኔታዎችን አላምዶ የሚኖር/ተላማጅ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Flexible, Adjustable, Adaptable\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Rigid, Inflexible\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Adaptive behavior enables individuals to deal effectively with daily challenges.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>15. Empowering (Adjective / Verb)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Making someone stronger and more confident, especially in controlling their life.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> አቅም የሚሰጥ፣ የሚያበቃ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Enabling, Authorizing, Strengthening\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Disempowering, Weakening\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Life skills are self-helping skills aimed at empowering people to reach their potential.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>16. Innate (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Inborn; natural rather than acquired by learning.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ተፈጥሯዊ፣ አብሮ የተወለደ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Inborn, Natural, Hereditary\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Acquired, Learned\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Everyone is born with an innate potential to belong to a family or culture.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>17. Aloof (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Not friendly or forthcoming; cool and distant.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ተለይቶ የሚኖር፣ ቀዝቀዝ ያለ/ያልተቀላቀለ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Detached, Distant, Unfriendly\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Friendly, Warm, Sociable\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> When the need for belonging is not met, a person may easily become aloof and self-centered.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>18. Reciprocal (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Given, felt, or done in return; mutual.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የጋራ፣ እርስ በእርስ የሚደረግ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Mutual, Shared, Complementary\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> One-sided, Unilateral\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Belonging allows a person to express social interest in a mutually reciprocal manner.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>19. Distorted (Verb / Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Pulled or twisted out of shape; misrepresented or damaged.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> የተዛባ፣ መልክ ያጣ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Twisted, Misrepresented, Warped\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Natural, Correct, Genuine\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Without the right opportunities, genetic needs can be distorted or destroyed.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>20. Prerequisite (Noun / Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> A thing that is required as a prior condition for something else to happen.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ቅድመ-ሁኔታ፣ አስፈላጊ መሠረት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Requirement, Precondition, Essential\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Optional, Voluntary\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> The fulfillment of belonging is a prerequisite for emotional well-being.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>21. Manipulative (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Exercising control or influence over somebody in a clever or dishonest way.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> አታላይ፣ ሰዎችን ለራሱ ጥቅምና ፍላጎት የሚጠቀም\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Calculating, Scheme-driven, Deceitful\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Honest, Sincere, Open\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Unmet social needs can cause an individual to become manipulative toward others.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>22. Self-centered (Adjective)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Preoccupied with oneself and one's own affairs; selfish.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ራሱን ብቻ የሚወድ / ራስ ወዳድ\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Selfish, Egocentric, Egoistic\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Altruistic, Unselfish, Caring\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> A lack of a sense of belonging often leads to self-centered behaviors.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>23. Assertiveness (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Confident and forceful behavior, expressing views clearly without aggression.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> በራስ የመተማመን/ግልጽ አቋም የመያዝ ብቃት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Confidence, Decisiveness, Self-assurance\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Passivity, Timidity, Hesitancy\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Assertiveness training helps students express their ideas clearly and defend their boundaries.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>24. Fulfillment (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> Satisfaction or happiness as a result of fully developing one's abilities or character.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> እርካታ፣ ስኬት፣ ፍላጎትን ማሟላት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Satisfaction, Attainment, Realization\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Dissatisfaction, Failure, Disappointment\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Responsible choices lead to personal happiness and maximum life fulfillment.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n<font color='#007BFF'><b>25. Conflict resolution (Noun)</b></font>\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>English:</b></font> The process by which two or more parties reach a peaceful agreement to a disagreement.\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Amharic:</b></font> ግጭት መፍታት\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Synonyms:</b></font> Dispute settlement, Reconciliation, Pacification\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Antonyms:</b></font> Conflict escalation, Confrontation\n• <font color='#28A745'><b>Example:</b></font> Life skills programs teach students decision-making and peaceful conflict resolution.\n\n───────────────────────────\n\n❤️\n<b><font color='#DC3545'>Dear EthioFresh Students! All 25 vocabulary terms for Skill 2 (Unit 1: Life Skills) are now 100% complete. Practice these terms thoroughly for your exams! 🙏✨</font></b>"
  }
]
